{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Dissatisfaction: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja65'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 65 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>5. Anabhiratijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Dissatisfaction: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yathā nadī ca pantho ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Just like rivers and roads, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pānāgāraṁ sabhā papā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>taverns, hotels, and pubs, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ lokitthiyo nāma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are those called women in the world. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nāsaṁ kujjhanti paṇḍitā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sages do not get angry with them. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Anabhiratijātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
